.TH BOOTSTRAP.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-batch-queues" "Mu2e DAQ Tools"
.SH NAME
bootstrap.sh \- set up the operator toolchain for mu2edaq-batch-queues
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./bootstrap.sh
.RB [ \-\-python
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-dev ]
.RB [ \-h ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates
.I ./venv
if it is missing, then installs or upgrades ansible-core, PyYAML, Jinja2 and
pytest in it. Also installs the Ansible Galaxy collections listed in
.I requirements.yml
into
.IR ./collections .
It is safe to re-run.
.PP
A Python 3.9 interpreter gets ansible-core 2.15; Python 3.10 or newer gets
2.17 or 2.18. The playbooks run on both.
.PP
On Windows 11, run
.B bootstrap.ps1
instead. It forwards to this script inside WSL2, because Ansible has no
native Windows control node.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-python " path"
Interpreter for the venv (environment
.BR PYTHON ,
default
.BR python3 ).
Must be 3.9 or newer.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-dev
Skip the test dependencies.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
\&./bootstrap.sh
PYTHON=python3.11 ./bootstrap.sh \-\-no\-dev
venv/bin/python \-m pytest \-q tests
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mc1-slurm-deploy (1)
